    "Full API spec": "include/Types.h:\n- struct Position { int x; int y; };\n- enum class Direction { Up, Down, Left, Right };\nSemantics: Position uses integer grid coordinates. Direction enumerates movement axes. This header is the sole definition site for both Position and Direction; any header using them must include this header directly.\n\ninclude/IRandom.h:\n- class IRandom { public: virtual ~IRandom() = default; virtual std::size_t next(std::size_t maxExclusive) = 0; };\n- class DefaultRandom final : public IRandom { public: explicit DefaultRandom(std::uint32_t seed); std::size_t next(std::size_t maxExclusive) override; private: std::mt19937 engine_; };\nSemantics: next(maxExclusive) returns an integer in [0, maxExclusive) uniformly. Behavior is deterministic given the seed. Header includes <cstddef>, <cstdint>, and <random> and uses std::size_t, std::uint32_t, std::mt19937.\n\ninclude/Board.h:\n- class Board { public: Board(std::size_t width, std::size_t height); std::size_t getWidth() const noexcept; std::size_t getHeight() const noexcept; bool inBounds(Position p) const noexcept; private: std::size_t width_; std::size_t height_; };\nSemantics: Stores immutable grid dimensions. inBounds returns true iff 0 <= p.x < width and 0 <= p.y < height.\n\ninclude/Snake.h:\n- class Snake { public: Snake(Position start, Direction dir, int initialLength); Position head() const; Position tail() const; const std::deque<Position>& body() const noexcept; Direction direction() const noexcept; bool trySetDirection(Direction d); void advanceTo(Position next, bool grow); bool occupies(Position p) const noexcept; private: std::deque<Position> body_; Direction dir_; };\nSemantics: Constructor initializes a length-3 body when called by Game as per protocol, extending opposite to initial direction. trySetDirection prevents 180-degree reversal relative to current direction; returns true if accepted, false if ignored. advanceTo moves head to 'next'; if grow is false, it pops the tail; if grow is true, it keeps the tail (growing by one). occupies checks if any segment equals p.\n\ninclude/Game.h:\n- class Game { public: Game(std::size_t width, std::size_t height, IRandom& rng); void reset(); void setDirection(Direction d); void tick(); bool isGameOver() const noexcept; std::size_t getScore() const noexcept; const Snake& getSnake() const noexcept; std::optional<Position> getFood() const; private: void placeFood(); bool wouldSelfCollide(Position next, bool grow) const; private: Board board_; IRandom& rng_; Snake snake_; std::optional<Position> food_; std::size_t score_; bool gameOver_; std::optional<Direction> pendingDir_; };\nSemantics:\n- Construction: validates dimensions (both width and height must be > 0; otherwise throws std::invalid_argument). Initializes the snake exactly as: snake_(Position{static_cast<int>(width / 2), static_cast<int>(height / 2)}, Direction::Right, 3). Resets score_=0, gameOver_=false, pendingDir_=std::nullopt, and places initial food on an unoccupied cell using RNG.\n- setDirection: queues a pending direction; actual change is applied at the start of the next tick via Snake::trySetDirection, preserving reversal-prevention.\n- tick: if gameOver_ is true, it is a no-op. Otherwise, applies pending direction, computes next head based on current direction, checks board_.inBounds(next) and self-collision via wouldSelfCollide(next, grow). Moving into the current tail position is allowed only when grow == false (i.e., not eating this tick). If next equals current food position, sets grow=true, advances snake with grow=true, increments score_, and calls placeFood(). Otherwise advances with grow=false. If out-of-bounds or self-collide, sets gameOver_=true and does not move further for this tick.\n- getFood returns std::nullopt if no food is currently placed (e.g., if board is fully occupied). placeFood selects uniformly among unoccupied cells using rng_.next().\n\nsrc/Random.cpp:\n- Implements DefaultRandom::DefaultRandom(seed) to seed engine_ and DefaultRandom::next(maxExclusive) using uniform_int_distribution in [0, maxExclusive-1]. Includes \"IRandom.h\" exactly.\n\nsrc/Board.cpp:\n- Implements Board methods; inBounds uses Position from include/Types.h (via include in include/Board.h).\n\nsrc/Snake.cpp:\n- Implements Snake, including reversal prevention in trySetDirection and growth-safe advanceTo.\n\nsrc/Game.cpp:\n- Implements Game: constructor performs validation, initializes snake_ exactly as specified, places food deterministically using rng_ over unoccupied cells, and ensures movement rules including the 'move into tail allowed only if not growing' rule via wouldSelfCollide.\n\nsrc/Main.cpp:\n- Demonstration-only thin runtime: constructs DefaultRandom with fixed seed, constructs Game, performs several ticks, prints a brief summary; no GUI/OS interactions. Not used by tests.\n\nInclude boundaries:\n- Any header using Position or Direction must include include/Types.h directly.\n- include/IRandom.h is the declaration site for both IRandom and DefaultRandom; src/Random.cpp includes only this header from the project.\n\nTesting boundaries:\n- tests/test_main.cpp includes only include/Game.h, include/IRandom.h, and include/Types.h, and links via the core library (not by including sources).",
    "Shared Knowledge": "Protocol mandates preserving exact file names and roles. Build file: CMakeLists.txt. Runtime entry: src/Main.cpp. Single test file: tests/test_main.cpp. Core types Position and Direction are defined only in include/Types.h; any header that mentions either must include include/Types.h directly. include/IRandom.h declares both IRandom and DefaultRandom and includes <cstddef>, <cstdint>, and <random>. src/Random.cpp includes \"IRandom.h\" exactly. include/Game.h includes \"Board.h\", \"IRandom.h\", \"Snake.h\", \"Types.h\", <cstddef>, <deque>, and <optional>. Direction reversal is prevented in Snake; food placement is deterministic using RNG over unoccupied cells; moving into tail is allowed only if not growing; Game constructor initializes snake_ exactly as specified. CMake builds a reusable core library from non-Main src/*.cpp, then links both the runtime (src/Main.cpp) and the test (tests/test_main.cpp) against that library. Tests include declared headers only and run via ctest.",
    "Execution Protocol": "Build with CMake and run ctest. Exactly one protocol-level test target is registered. tests/test_main.cpp includes declared headers only (no src/*.cpp). Both the runtime executable (src/Main.cpp) and the test executable (tests/test_main.cpp) link against the core library built from non-Main sources. No GUI or OS-specific behavior; tests are deterministic and headless.",
    "Anything UNCLEAR": ""
}
